# __PROJECT_TITLE__

A [PyLara](https://pypi.org/project/pylara/) application.

## Getting started

```bash
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate            # Windows   (Linux/macOS: source .venv/bin/activate)
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m manage migrate
python -m manage serve
```

Open http://127.0.0.1:8000.

## Everyday commands

```bash
python -m manage route:list                  # list routes
python -m manage make:controller PostController --resource
python -m manage make:model Post -m          # model + migration
python -m manage migrate                     # run migrations
python -m manage migrate:rollback            # undo the last batch
python -m unittest discover -v               # run the tests
```

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `app/controllers`, `app/models`, `app/middleware`, `app/providers` | Application code |
| `bootstrap/app.py` | Builds the application (database, providers, routes) |
| `routes/web.py`, `routes/api.py` | Route definitions |
| `resources/views` | HTML templates |
| `public` | Static files served at `/` (e.g. `public/css/app.css` -> `/css/app.css`) |
| `database/migrations` | Schema migrations |
| `config` | JSON configuration (`app.config.get("app.name")`) |
| `storage` | SQLite database and other runtime files |
| `.env` | Environment settings (never commit this file) |

Full documentation: see the PyLara docs.
